←: Snake: also watch the D-pad's own chrome for resize, not just the container (#23/#32) Real bug: board over-zoomed with the D-pad off-screen after rotating right after a game-over, self-correcting only by starting a new game. The fit reads the D-pad's own bounding rects, which settle via a separate listener ([REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO] -> setupMobileControls) not ordered relative to the board's own resize observer -- a game in progress papers over a bad ordering because the next automatic tick() refits again, but game-over stops that timer, leaving a fit landed against stale D-pad geometry with nothing left to ever retry it. Observing the D-pad's own chrome elements too means their real settled geometry is what triggers the correcting refit, regardless of whether a game happens to be running.


