2. **Same-clef notehead coloring** — uses VexFlow's `setKeyStyle(memberIndex, ...)` for true per-key styling (confirmed `setKeyStyle` actually exists in the vendored VexFlow build, so this isn't silently falling back), with the whole-note style kept as a fallback for older builds. New test directly asserts both a red and a green notehead render in the same chord.
