### 2026-08-30T12:40:08.673Z | codex | codex | conversation 01a04e07-94d6-7832-9230-353fae598034

No—not fully. I overstated them as current commitments.

- “Never interrupt an ongoing performance”: not met. A wrong note schedules an automatic replay, and `playTargetSequence()` can interrupt continued playing after the delay. [melody.js:1271]([REDACTED_PERSON])

- “Continue the guide while tracking missed and extra notes”: only partially met. Notes played during demonstration are queued, but they are evaluated afterward; the child cannot currently play continuously alongside the guide. [melody.js:1082]([REDACTED_PERSON])

- “Obvious target, voluntary replay/isolation”: partially met. The target and upcoming regions are visible, but replay is still automatically triggered after mistakes. There are no explicit replay/isolate controls yet.

- “Adaptive tolerance”: partially met. Chord members receive partial credit and recovery delay backs off, but pitch matching remains exact, timing feedback does not yet affect acceptance, and tolerance is not progressively tightened by level.

